      "title": "Reddit Deep Dive: Early Innings on a 20-Year-Old Platform",
      "fund": "r/ValueInvesting",
      "date": "March 2026",
      "summary": "This deep dive details Reddit's financial transformation, highlighting top-line revenue tripling over three years driven by a still-maturing ad stack featuring nascent tools like CAPI, Shopping Ads, and Dynamic Product Ads. The author models massive operating leverage from flat headcount growth and 90%+ gross margins, projecting substantial long-term ARPU expansion toward Meta's benchmarks. Valued at ~12.1x EV/Sales and 31.5x EV/Adjusted EBITDA, the post presents a strong long-term compounding thesis despite stock-based compensation drag.",
      "url": "https://www.reddit.com/r/ValueInvesting/search/?q=RDDT&restrict_sr=1&sort=top",
      "btn_label": "Reddit DDs \u2197"
    },
    {
      "title": "RDDT: Structuraly mispriced, with Q1 2026 actuals already 3% above Q1 2027 consensus",
      "fund": "r/ValueInvesting",
      "date": "May 2026",
      "summary": "This thesis argues that Wall Street sell-side analysts structurally underestimate Reddit's operating leverage, pointing to Q1 2026 incremental net income margins hitting 65.7% against market models expecting margin stagnation at ~30%. Key operational catalysts include AI data licensing renewals and settlements with OpenAI, Google, Anthropic, and Perplexity, alongside potential S&P 500 inclusion. With minimal capex requirements ($1M in Q1 2026) and free community moderation, the author projects multi-quarter EPS beats over conservative consensus.",
      "url": "https://www.reddit.com/r/ValueInvesting/search/?q=RDDT&restrict_sr=1&sort=top",
      "btn_label": "Reddit DDs \u2197"
    },
    {
      "title": "Reddit Deep Dive (RDDT): From Chronic Money-Loser To Cash Machine",
      "fund": "Substack / Investor's Compass",
      "date": "May 2026",
      "summary": "The analysis explores Reddit's sudden inflection from two decades of unprofitability to printing cash at a 47% free cash flow margin ($311M FCF on $663M revenue in Q1 2026). The thesis highlights Reddit's unique user-generated data moat against AI slop, strong digital ad stack expansion, and high ROE/ROA trajectories supported by a net-cash balance sheet. While rating the stock Market Perform solely due to short-term technical resistance, the author establishes a high-conviction fundamental case for multi-year compounding.",
      "url": "https://investorscompass.substack.com/archive?sort=search&search=RDDT",
      "btn_label": "Substack Archive \u2197"
    },
